The '''Cat Shrine''' (にゃんこ神社 ''Nyanko Jinja'') is a feature added to the [[Gamatoto Expedition]] menu in the [[Version 9.9 Update]] of the [[Nyanko Daisensou|Japanese Version]] and the [[Version 9.10 Update]] of the [[The Battle Cats|English Version]]. [[File:Shrine 001.png|thumb|right]]

If [[Into the Future]] Chapter 3 has been completed, the Cat Shrine will appear on the left side of the Gamatoto Expedition screen at random times, with a similar pattern to [[Zombie Outbreaks]]. When the Cat Shrine is available, the player can tap on it and be shown several options to donate XP to [[The Cat God]] in exchange for blessings, being [[Ototo Corps|materials]], [[Catfruit]], [[Catseye]]s or miscellaneous items, depending on the amount of XP donated. If enough time is elapsed without making an offering, the Cat Shrine will temporarily disappear.

The Cat Shrine will level up as the player donates XP; for every 10 levels, the Cat Shrine will temporarily disappear and gain a new design when it returns. Unlike [[Gamatoto Expedition|GAMATOTO]]'s costumes, which the player can cycle through, the Cat Shrine's appearance changes are permanent and cannot be configured. The current maximum level is 70, which requires the player to donate 575,600,000 XP.

As of [[Version 10.0 Update|Version 10.0]], the Cat Shrine also has a '''Cat Fortune''' (にゃんこみくじ ''Nyanko Mikuji'') option available, indicated by a speech bubble with a lantern and fortune slip next to the Cat Shrine. When Cat Fortunes are available, the player can spend 5 XP once to have their fortune told, providing flavor text and a chance to find a large Item Pack called a Great Fortune or summon Inari, a one-use GAMATOTO helper which doubles the non-[[Cat Food]] rewards found during an expedition. When Cat Fortunes are unavailable, the Cat Fortune button will be greyed out and provide the text "The fortune slip box is empty..." when tapped. XP spent on fortune slips does not count toward Cat Shrine levels.

