==Notes==
*There are four types of offerings costing different amounts of XP. Each type of offering can only be made five times per Cat Shrine appearance. Modest offerings are notably the one of the few sources of the elusive Gold Catfruit, which can unlock rare and valuable [[True Form]]s such as [[Gold Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Gold Cat]]'s. Interestingly, there is also a guarantee system where you will gain one Gold Catfruit every 30 donations of 1 million XP each (these do not need to be consecutive, and getting a Gold Catfruit from the 1% chance does not reset the counter).

==Trivia==
*On occasion, the Cat God from [[The Burgle Cats]] can be seen behind the Cat Shrine.
*The Cat Shrine resembles a ''[[wikipedia:Hokora|hokora]]'', a miniature Shinto shrine.
*[[wikipedia:Inari Ōkami|Inari Ōkami]], or just Inari, is the Japanese ''[[wikipedia:Kami|kami]]'' of foxes, fertility, rice, agriculture, industry, and worldly success, to whom many have made offerings at her own [[wikipedia:Inari shrine|shrines]].
*Cat Fortunes are based on ''[[wikipedia:O-mikuji|omikuji]]'', fortune-telling slips found at Shinto shrines and Buddhist temples in Japan.
*The level-up quote "You are filled with determination." is a reference to the indie role-playing game ''[[wikipedia:Undertale|Undertale]]'', in which the same phrase appears whenever the player uses a save point.
*The Cat Fortune "The 7 Orbs shall grant all your wishes." is a reference to the series ''[[wikipedia:Dragon Ball|Dragon Ball]]''.

